            <ArticleTitle>Utility of intravascular ultrasound in the diagnosis of ambiguous calcific left main stenoses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>385</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Advances in coronary angiographic imaging have been recently realized with the advent of so-called flat panel technology. However, some of the limitations of coronary angiography, including the so-called pseudo-thrombus appearance of focal highly calcific coronary artery lesions remain. This case highlights the utility of intravascular ultrasound in determining the pathobiology of coronary artery lesions in select cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
